 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Сюрприз для всех  (A Surprise for Everyone)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "vika": "Вика"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max has plans for the evening. Vika is waiting for him at home for a quiet dinner, but he has brought his friends along as a surprise. We'll hear their phone call in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Макс, ну ты где?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты скоро?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я уже здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Почему ты там стоишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я жду своих друзей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Каких друзей?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Настю и Костю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты их позвал сюда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, это сюрприз.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Я не готова к гостям.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Всё будет хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Заходи быстрее.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back over the phone call, slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Макс, ну ты где?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Max, where are you?' \"Nu\" adds impatience, and \"ty gde?\" is literally \"you where?\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты скоро?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Will you be long?' \"Ty skoro?\" is literally \"you soon?\", with no word for coming at all.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я уже здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm already here.' \"Uzhe\" means already, and \"zdes\" means here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Почему ты там стоишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why are you standing there?' \"Stoish\" comes from \"stoyat\", to stand, the word Barinov barked earlier.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я жду своих друзей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm waiting for my friends.' \"Zhdu\", I'm waiting, takes the friends straight after it, with no \"for\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Каких друзей?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What friends?' \"Kakikh druzey\" copies the ending of \"svoikh druzey\" in Max's line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Настю и Костю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nastya and Kostya.' Both names switch \"-ya\" to \"-yu\", since they're still the people being waited for.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты их позвал сюда?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you invite them here?' \"Pozval\", called over, comes from \"zvat\", to call. \"Ikh\" means them.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, это сюрприз.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, it's a surprise.' \"Syurpriz\" is borrowed from French, like many party words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Я не готова к гостям.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm not ready for guests.' \"Gotova\", ready, ends in \"-a\" for a woman. \"K gostyam\" is \"for guests\", literally \"towards guests\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Всё будет хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everything will be fine.' \"Vsyo budet khorosho\" is the classic Russian reassurance.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Заходи быстрее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hurry up and come in.' \"Zakhodi\" is \"come in\", and \"bystree\", faster, turns it into \"hurry up\". Now the phone call once more, without a break.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Макс, ну ты где?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты скоро?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я уже здесь.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Почему ты там стоишь?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я жду своих друзей.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Каких друзей?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Настю и Костю.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты их позвал сюда?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, это сюрприз.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Я не готова к гостям.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Всё будет хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Заходи быстрее.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Vika is not ready for guests, and Max is about to find out how much. \"Vsyo budet khorosho\", everything will be fine, is what Russians say right before it isn't. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
